# Bundled data notices

## HPO README fixture

`extdata/hpo-readme.obo` is a small derived fixture containing selected term
identifiers, labels, aliases, definitions, and relationships from the Human
Phenotype Ontology (HPO), <https://hpo.jax.org/>. It is included solely to run
the README without a network download. HPO is available under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0); see
<https://hpo.jax.org/app/license>.

## Mondo subset

`extdata/mondo-subset.obo` contains three selected complete term stanzas from
Mondo v2026-10-06, published by the Monarch Initiative and Mondo contributors:
<https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/releases/tag/v2026-10-06>.
The fixture retains a reduced release-identifying header. The terms and their
annotations are unchanged. The upstream ontology is licensed CC BY 4.0;
`MONDO-LICENSE` contains the license text. `extdata/source-releases.csv`
records the upstream file digest, fixture digest, and selected identifiers.

## DisMech record

`extdata/dismech-marfan.yaml` is the verbatim Marfan Syndrome record from
<https://github.com/monarch-initiative/dismech> at commit
`fac61860115b1fdb194de4f4cacef3a8f6a398af`. Its pinned source URI and digest
are in `extdata/source-releases.csv`. `DISMECH-LICENSE` retains the upstream
BSD 3-Clause copyright notice, conditions, and disclaimer. The fixture's
availability timestamp records observation of the public artifact; it is not
a claim about the commit's original publication time.

## Native extension

`extension/` contains the canonical DuckSemantics C extension sources and
DuckDB C API headers. `extension/duckdb_capi/LICENSE` retains the DuckDB
Foundation's MIT notice for the headers. The synthetic GGUF parser and tokenizer fixtures in
`extdata/` are generated by the extension's C fixture builders and contain
no trained weights.
